{"kind":"report","text":"RULING: keep every merge-published successor resting directly on the sealed merge receipt. Do not re-anchor it to a ratified decision, and do not weaken the fresh-bases discipline to live-not-retired.\n\nFreshness is restored by a temporal Workroom-fold rule on the direct receipt-to-published-successor edge. For a genuine successor published by that receipt, ordinary staleness causes already active at or before the receipt's own sequence are settled by the merge and do not make the successor stale at birth. Any active relevant cause arising after the receipt still propagates. Direct retirement of the receipt still flares the successor. The receipt remains historically stale when that is true; only its published successor begins a new current implementation epoch.\n\nThis exception is narrow and fail-closed. It applies only when the fold recognizes an effective valid merge receipt and plan, the artifact cites that receipt directly, the artifact is at the receipt's exact merge_head and a declared exact successor path, and the publication is otherwise genuine. An unrelated record that merely cites a receipt gains no exemption. Implementation needs a dated ordinary-cause computation, including undated fail-closed handling: comparing stale-now with stale-as-of-receipt is insufficient when old and new causes coexist.\n\ndescribes_superseded_world is unchanged. World staleness already present at the verdict continues to invalidate merge authority; post-verdict moved-world news remains recorded under the existing temporal rule; direct artifact-to-artifact provenance and a later condemned succession chain continue to flare. The repair settles only ordinary reasoning already accounted for at merge publication.\n\nOwnership is layer 5, the Workroom application interpreter. Enforce it in internal/workroom/fold.go's staleness computation and projection, not in the kernel and not solely in gs. The CLI continues only to validate and construct the signed receipt and successors. Bump the Workroom fold/profile version, rebuild cache compatibility coverage, document the contract in docs/reference/architecture.md and docs/reference/gs/merge.md, and test stale-at-birth restoration, mixed old-plus-new causes, later approval and receipt retirement, unrelated receipt borrowers, world-stale chains, and condemned successions.\n\nThe left-live and paired-field receipt contracts do not change. merge_left_live and merge_changed_paths remain the existing optional paired extension; they still govern snapshot accounting, sibling protection, abandoned debt, and unaccounted-successor warnings. Historical receipts without the pair retain their parsing/accounting semantics. The freshness checkpoint neither grants retirement authority nor changes the receipt plan, live/retired state, or left-live classification. Implement this only through a child request on then-current bases.","body":{"conclusion":"temporal receipt-to-successor checkpoint in Workroom fold; fresh-bases discipline unchanged; implementation deferred to child request"}}